{%- comment -%}
  Packaging ritual — Nolan Barret–style sticky object storytelling (a Bureau-Nine-influenced,
  Amber-cinematic take, dressed entirely in CAVIERA's own six-step packaging ritual, not a
  photographic-object study): one anchored visual stage at desktop beside the six-step story
  (Arrive/Open/Discover/Unseal/Reveal/Keep); as the reader scrolls the story, the stage's own
  content changes to represent whichever stage is closest to the reading focus. Mobile drops the
  shared sticky stage (a side-by-side sticky panel doesn't hold up in a single column) in favour of
  each stage carrying its own compact inline visual, right beside its own copy.

  SCROLL-ANIMATION REBUILD (this task): the section already had a sticky visual-stage column
  (.caviera-ritual__stage-col, sticky at 1024px+) and an active-step controller
  (assets/caviera-packaging-ritual.js) — refined rather than duplicated. Three real gaps, closed:
  1. The stage never actually changed per step — one image (or one static "material composition")
     sat there for the whole section, with only a small scale nudge at "Unseal". Now every stage
     block gets its own real visual state (data-stage-kind, crossfaded exactly like Object in
     Focus's own data-active-chapter/data-state-index system — see caviera-home.css), matched by
     the step's own title text ("contains 'arrive'", etc. — the same content-matching technique
     already used below for the House Seal placement), not by block position, so reordering or
     renaming a step keeps the right visual attached to it.
  2. The active-step detection reused the same IntersectionObserver threshold/rootMargin combination
     (threshold: 0.5, rootMargin: '-40% 0px -40% 0px') already found and fixed elsewhere in this
     project (assets/caviera-house-codes.js's own fix note) — geometrically unreliable once a step's
     height is a meaningful fraction of the viewport. Replaced with the same deterministic
     "closest step centre to a fixed viewport focal line" rAF calculation already proven in
     assets/caviera-object-focus.js.
  3. Real packaging photography does not exist yet for any stage. Rather than an obviously-
     placeholder single "material composition" box, each of the six kinds now gets its OWN
     elegant CAVIERA material-study fallback (brand colour fields, the approved House Seal for
     Unseal, and — Reveal only — the same bundled jewellery photograph already used as the hero's
     and Object in Focus's own bundled default, assets/15_oryx_necklace_on_model.png) — see
     snippets/caviera-ritual-stage-visual.liquid, shared by both the desktop stage and the mobile
     inline media so this logic exists in exactly one place. A merchant's own "Stage image" on any
     step block always wins over its fallback, per block, independent of the others.

  House Seal placement: the small mark beside the step copy (not the stage's own visual) still
  matches whichever step is titled "Unseal" (case-insensitive) — unchanged from before.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign has_steps = false
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.settings.title != blank
      assign has_steps = true
    endif
  endfor

  assign mark_mode = 'light'
  unless section.settings.color_scheme == 'bone'
    assign mark_mode = 'dark'
  endunless

  assign first_kind = 'arrive'
  assign found_first_kind = false
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.settings.title != blank and found_first_kind == false
      assign title_down = block.settings.title | downcase
      if title_down contains 'arrive'
        assign first_kind = 'arrive'
      elsif title_down contains 'open'
        assign first_kind = 'open'
      elsif title_down contains 'discover'
        assign first_kind = 'discover'
      elsif title_down contains 'unseal'
        assign first_kind = 'unseal'
      elsif title_down contains 'reveal'
        assign first_kind = 'reveal'
      elsif title_down contains 'keep'
        assign first_kind = 'keep'
      else
        assign first_kind = 'arrive'
      endif
      assign found_first_kind = true
    endif
  endfor
-%}
<section class="caviera-section caviera-ritual" data-scheme="{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}" data-spacing="{{ section.settings.spacing | default: 'standard' }}">
  <div class="container container--narrow caviera-ritual__head" data-reveal>
    {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}<span class="eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</span>{%- endif -%}
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}<h2 class="heading-h1 caviera-ritual__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>{%- endif -%}
    {%- if section.settings.supporting_copy != blank -%}<p class="body-text caviera-ritual__intro-copy">{{ section.settings.supporting_copy }}</p>{%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <div class="container caviera-ritual__body">
    {%- if has_steps -%}
    <div class="caviera-ritual__stage-col" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- comment -%}
        Desktop only — hidden below 1024px, see caviera-home.css. aria-hidden: a decorative,
        atmospheric echo of the ordered list beside it, which already narrates the full ritual in
        text (and, for "Unseal"/"Reveal", already carries its own accessible copy) — without this,
        assistive tech would hit all six stacked states here before ever reaching that list.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="caviera-ritual__stage" data-active-kind="{{ first_kind }}">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign title_down = block.settings.title | downcase
              assign kind = 'arrive'
              if title_down contains 'arrive'
                assign kind = 'arrive'
              elsif title_down contains 'open'
                assign kind = 'open'
              elsif title_down contains 'discover'
                assign kind = 'discover'
              elsif title_down contains 'unseal'
                assign kind = 'unseal'
              elsif title_down contains 'reveal'
                assign kind = 'reveal'
              elsif title_down contains 'keep'
                assign kind = 'keep'
              endif
            -%}
            <div class="caviera-ritual__stage-state" data-stage-kind="{{ kind }}">
              {%- render 'caviera-ritual-stage-visual', kind: kind, image: block.settings.image, mark_mode: mark_mode, label: block.settings.title -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="caviera-ritual__rail">
      {%- if has_steps -%}
        <span class="caviera-ritual__progress" aria-hidden="true"><span class="caviera-ritual__progress-fill" data-ritual-progress-fill></span></span>
        <ol class="caviera-ritual__steps" data-ritual-steps>
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign title_down = block.settings.title | downcase
                assign kind = 'arrive'
                if title_down contains 'arrive'
                  assign kind = 'arrive'
                elsif title_down contains 'open'
                  assign kind = 'open'
                elsif title_down contains 'discover'
                  assign kind = 'discover'
                elsif title_down contains 'unseal'
                  assign kind = 'unseal'
                elsif title_down contains 'reveal'
                  assign kind = 'reveal'
                elsif title_down contains 'keep'
                  assign kind = 'keep'
                endif
                assign is_unseal = false
                if kind == 'unseal'
                  assign is_unseal = true
                endif
              -%}
              <li class="caviera-ritual__step" data-stage-kind="{{ kind }}" data-reveal {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <span class="caviera-ritual__step-number label" aria-hidden="true">{% if forloop.index < 10 %}0{% endif %}{{ forloop.index }}</span>
                <div class="caviera-ritual__step-copy">
                  <h3 class="caviera-ritual__step-title">{{ block.settings.title }}</h3>
                  {%- comment -%}
                    Mobile only (hidden at 1024px+, see caviera-home.css) — each stage carries its
                    own compact visual right beside its own copy, rather than one shared sticky
                    stage; a side-by-side sticky panel doesn't hold up in a single mobile column.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <div class="caviera-ritual__step-media">
                    {%- render 'caviera-ritual-stage-visual', kind: kind, image: block.settings.image, mark_mode: mark_mode, label: block.settings.title -%}
                  </div>
                  {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}<p class="body-text">{{ block.settings.body }}</p>{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if is_unseal and section.settings.show_seal -%}
                    <span class="caviera-ritual__step-seal">{%- render 'caviera-house-seal', mode: mark_mode, width: 32, alt: '' -%}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ol>
      {%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
        <div class="caviera-editor-note">Add up to six ritual steps as blocks.</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script src="{{ 'caviera-packaging-ritual.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Packaging ritual",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Label", "default": "Packaging" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "A ritual, not a box." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "supporting_copy", "label": "Supporting line", "default": "The experience moves from protection to intimacy, with one controlled House cue at each stage." },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Colour", "default": "obsidian",
      "options": [
        { "value": "bone", "label": "Warm Bone" },
        { "value": "cinnabar", "label": "Cinnabar" },
        { "value": "obsidian", "label": "Obsidian" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "spacing", "label": "Section spacing", "default": "standard",
      "options": [
        { "value": "compact", "label": "Compact" },
        { "value": "standard", "label": "Standard" },
        { "value": "spacious", "label": "Spacious" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_seal", "label": "Show House Seal beside the \"Unseal\" step", "default": true, "info": "Matches whichever step block is titled \"Unseal\" (case-insensitive) — rename that step and the mark moves with it." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "step",
      "name": "Step",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title", "info": "e.g. Arrive, Open, Discover, Unseal, Reveal, Keep" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Description", "info": "One to two short sentences read best." },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Stage image", "info": "Real packaging/product photography for this exact stage only. Leave blank to use the CAVIERA material-study fallback for this stage instead (never a placeholder box)." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Packaging ritual",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "title": "Arrive", "body": "Protection first. An Obsidian outer layer keeps the object concealed until the ritual begins." } },
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "title": "Open", "body": "Cinnabar appears within — the House colour, held in reserve until this moment." } },
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "title": "Discover", "body": "Warm Bone softens the interior and brings the object into a more intimate field." } },
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "title": "Unseal", "body": "The House Seal marks the threshold between packaging and object." } },
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "title": "Reveal", "body": "The jewellery stands alone, with nothing competing for attention." } },
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "title": "Keep", "body": "The presentation is designed to remain part of the ownership experience." } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
